  fill: #ff0000; /* Change the fill color to red on hover */
}
```

This will change the fill color of the SVG to red when the user hovers over it. You can replace `#ff0000` with any other color you like.

If you want to add a more complex hover effect, you can use CSS to change the stroke color, stroke width, or even add a new path or shape on hover. For example:

```css
svg {
  transition: fill 0.2s ease-in-out, stroke 0.2s ease-in-out;
}

