  fill: #ff0000;
  stroke: #00ff00; /* Change the stroke color to green on hover */
  stroke-width: 2px; /* Increase the stroke width on hover */
}
```

You can also use CSS animations to create a more complex hover effect. For example:

```css
svg {
  transition: fill 0.2s ease-in-out;
}

svg:hover {
  fill: #ff0000;
  animation: hover-effect 0.5s ease-in-out;
}

@keyframes hover-effect {
  0% {
    fill: #ff0000;
  }
  100% {
    fill: #00ff00;
  }
}
```

This will create a smooth animation that changes the fill color from red to green on hover.

